_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Inverted WSL detection logic renders this function ineffective.**

On WSL, `process.platform` returns `'linux'`, not `'win32'`. Therefore, `isWindows` is `false` and `isWsl()` exits immediately at line 30-32, never reaching the actual WSL detection logic. This function will always return `false` on real WSL systems.

The code currently works by accident because `canRunShell = !isWindows || isWsl()` short-circuits on WSL (since `!isWindows` is already `true`). However, this should be corrected for clarity and to prevent future bugs if the logic changes.



Apply this diff to fix the logic:

```diff
 function isWsl() {
-  if (!isWindows) {
+  if (isWindows) {
     return false;
   }

   if (process.env.WSL_DISTRO_NAME || process.env.WSL_INTEROP) {
     return true;
   }

   try {
     const version = require('fs').readFileSync('/proc/version', 'utf8').toLowerCase();
     return version.includes('microsoft');
   } catch {
     return false;
   }
 }
```

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In code/core/src/core-server/utils/open-browser/opener.ts around lines 29 to 44,
the initial platform check is inverted so the function returns early on WSL;
change the guard from "if (!isWindows) return false" to "if (isWindows) return
false" so native Windows exits early and non-Windows (including WSL) proceeds to
the WSL detection logic (env vars and /proc/version), leaving the rest of the
function unchanged.
```

</details>

